{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '850,1530p'\"","aggregated_output":"   850\t\n   851\t(defn- attempt-id\n   852\t  [ctx counter]\n   853\t  [(get-in ctx [:incarnation :yin.expander/token]) counter])\n   854\t\n   855\t\n   856\t(defn macro-entry\n   857\t  \"A macro-store value: a self-contained lambda tree `packet` with the AST\n   858\t   `contract` it was produced under. The store holds only these. The\n   859\t   transformer runner verifies the contract before it executes the packet\n   860\t   (Rule R: a persistent or supplied code packet is never relabelled), and\n   861\t   the expander stamps only what it harvests itself, under\n   862\t   `vm/ast-contract`.\"\n   863\t  [packet contract]\n   864\t  {:yin.macro/tree packet, :yin.macro/contract contract})\n   865\t\n   866\t\n   867\t(defn- verified-tree\n   868\t  \"The packet of a macro-store value after its contract is verified\n   869\t   against `vm/ast-contract`: `:contract-missing` for a bare packet or an\n   870\t   entry without one, `:contract-mismatch` for an old stamp.\"\n   871\t  [entry]\n   872\t  (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract\n   873\t                      (when (map? entry) (:yin.macro/contract entry)))\n   874\t  (:yin.macro/tree entry))\n   875\t\n   876\t\n   877\t(defn- check-store!\n   878\t  \"A supplied macro store: no reserved name is a macro (Rule R), and every\n   879\t   entry carries the current AST contract. Returns `store`.\"\n   880\t  [store]\n   881\t  (vm/check-bindings! :macro store)\n   882\t  (doseq [entry (vals store)] (verified-tree entry))\n   883\t  store)\n   884\t\n   885\t\n   886\t(defn- invoke*\n   887\t  \"Run one macro body. `entry` is a macro-store value (`macro-entry`),\n   888\t   verified before anything runs. `counter` is the attempt counter, which\n   889\t   gensyms read. `{:tree packet}` or `{:error e}`.\"\n   890\t  [entry operands ctx counter]\n   891\t  (let [macro-tree (verified-tree entry)\n   892\t        macro-root (first macro-tree)\n   893\t        params (nth (root-row macro-tree) 2)\n   894\t        {:keys [env expected got]} (bind-arguments params operands)]\n   895\t    (if-not env\n   896\t      {:error {:kind :arity, :macro macro-root, :expected expected, :got got}}\n   897\t      (let [n (volatile! 0)\n   898\t            token (get-in ctx [:incarnation :yin.expander/token])\n   899\t            gensym (fn [prefix]\n   900\t                     (let [i @n]\n   901\t                       (vswap! n inc)\n   902\t                       (symbol (str (if (symbol? prefix) (name prefix) prefix)\n   903\t                                    \"__\" token \"_\" counter \"_\" i))))\n   904\t            run (or (:eval ctx) bounded-row-evaluator)\n   905\t            {:keys [value error]} (run {:macro-tree macro-tree,\n   906\t                                        :contract (:yin.macro/contract entry),\n   907\t                                        :env env,\n   908\t                                        :prelude (prelude gensym),\n   909\t                                        :max-steps (get-in ctx [:guards :max-steps])})]\n   910\t        (if error\n   911\t          {:error (assoc error :macro macro-root)}\n   912\t          {:tree value})))))\n   913\t\n   914\t\n   915\t(def default-guards\n   916\t  {:max-depth 100,\n   917\t   :max-rows-per-expansion 10000,\n   918\t   :max-rows-per-batch nil,\n   919\t   :max-steps 100000})\n   920\t\n   921\t\n   922\t(defn invoke\n   923\t  \"Run `entry`, a macro-store value (`macro-entry`: a self-contained lambda\n   924\t   packet and its AST contract), on `operand-trees` and return its result\n   925\t   tree packet, unvalidated. The contract is verified first\n   926\t   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`, thrown). Gensyms use\n   927\t   `(:attempt ctx)` as the attempt counter. Throws `ex-info` carrying the\n   928\t   error data on an arity, guard, suspension, or body failure.\"\n   929\t  [entry operand-trees ctx]\n   930\t  (let [ctx (update ctx :guards #(merge default-guards %))\n   931\t        {:keys [tree error]} (invoke* entry (vec operand-trees) ctx\n   932\t                                      (:attempt ctx))]\n   933\t    (when error\n   934\t      (throw (ex-info \"Macro invocation failed\" error)))\n   935\t    tree))\n   936\t\n   937\t\n   938\t;; =============================================================================\n   939\t;; Tail marking and lowering (§6, §3.2 steps 6-7)\n   940\t;; =============================================================================\n   941\t\n   942\t(defn- retail\n   943\t  \"Recompute every `tail?` slot below `root`, in context `tail?`, over a\n   944\t   working index; `[index' root']`. Tail-ness is contextual, so one shared\n   945\t   row in two contexts becomes two rows.\"\n   946\t  [index root]\n   947\t  (let [memo (volatile! {})]\n   948\t    (letfn [(go\n   949\t              [index a tail?]\n   950\t              (if-let [hit (get @memo [a tail?])]\n   951\t                [index hit]\n   952\t                (let [row (get index a)\n   953\t                      tag (row-tag row)\n   954\t                      ctxs (case tag\n   955\t                             :lambda [true]\n   956\t                             :if [false tail? tail?]\n   957\t                             (repeat false))\n   958\t                      [index children']\n   959\t                      (reduce (fn [[index acc] [[_ c] t]]\n   960\t                                (let [[index c'] (go index c t)]\n   961\t                                  [index (conj acc c')]))\n   962\t                              [index []]\n   963\t                              (map vector (child-places row) ctxs))\n   964\t                      [index a'] (rebuild-row index row children')\n   965\t                      [index a'] (if (and (= :application tag)\n   966\t                                          (not= tail? (nth (get index a') 4)))\n   967\t                                   (intern-body index (assoc (subvec (get index a') 1) 3 tail?))\n   968\t                                   [index a'])]\n   969\t                  (vswap! memo assoc [a tail?] a')\n   970\t                  [index a'])))]\n   971\t      (go index root true))))\n   972\t\n   973\t\n   974\t(defn mark-tail\n   975\t  \"Recompute all observable tail slots of a tree packet, setting and\n   976\t   clearing marks (§6): the root is in tail context, an `:if` test is\n   977\t   non-tail and its branches inherit, application operators and operands are\n   978\t   non-tail, a lambda body is tail, and every other child is non-tail.\"\n   979\t  [packet]\n   980\t  (let [[index root] (retail (packet-index packet) (first packet))]\n   981\t    (packet-of index root)))\n   982\t\n   983\t\n   984\t(defn- lower-standins\n   985\t  \"Replace every stand-in by the canonical literal of its name.\"\n   986\t  [index root]\n   987\t  (let [memo (volatile! {})]\n   988\t    (letfn [(go\n   989\t              [index a]\n   990\t              (if-let [hit (get @memo a)]\n   991\t                [index hit]\n   992\t                (let [row (get index a)\n   993\t                      [index a']\n   994\t                      (if (= standin-tag (row-tag row))\n   995\t                        (intern-body index [:literal (nth row 2)])\n   996\t                        (let [[index children']\n   997\t                              (reduce (fn [[index acc] [_ c]]\n   998\t                                        (let [[index c'] (go index c)]\n   999\t                                          [index (conj acc c')]))\n  1000\t                                      [index []]\n  1001\t                                      (child-places row))]\n  1002\t                          (rebuild-row index row children')))]\n  1003\t                  (vswap! memo assoc a a')\n  1004\t                  [index a'])))]\n  1005\t      (go index root))))\n  1006\t\n  1007\t\n  1008\t;; =============================================================================\n  1009\t;; Harvest and post-harvest (§3.2 steps 2, 3, 5; §3.5)\n  1010\t;; =============================================================================\n  1011\t\n  1012\t(defn- harvest\n  1013\t  \"Initial harvest: iterate definitions in ordinal order; a declared one\n  1014\t   installs its lambda packet, a plain one removes the name. Last wins.\n  1015\t   A reserved name is never a definition key or a macro name (Rule R).\"\n  1016\t  [store index-of definitions]\n  1017\t  (reduce (fn [store {:keys [tree name value declared?]}]\n  1018\t            (when (vm/reserved-name? name)\n  1019\t              (vm/refuse-reserved! :definition-key name))\n  1020\t            (if declared?\n  1021\t              (assoc store name\n  1022\t                     (macro-entry (packet-of (index-of tree) value)\n  1023\t                                  vm/ast-contract))\n  1024\t              (dissoc store name)))\n  1025\t          store\n  1026\t          definitions))\n  1027\t\n  1028\t\n  1029\t(defn- post-harvest\n  1030\t  \"The next batch's store: start from the store before initial harvest and\n  1031\t   walk the final occurrence tree in declaration order — for an application\n  1032\t   whose operator is a lambda, operands left to right then the lambda body;\n  1033\t   otherwise child slots in grammar order. A plain definition removes its\n  1034\t   name; a stand-in whose `k` exists and whose catalogue name matches\n  1035\t   installs that entry; later occurrences win.\"\n  1036\t  [store index root catalogue]\n  1037\t  (letfn [(children\n  1038\t            [row]\n  1039\t            (let [places (child-places row)]\n  1040\t              (if (and (= :application (row-tag row))\n  1041\t                       (= :lambda (row-tag (get index (nth row 2)))))\n  1042\t                (concat (map second (rest places))\n  1043\t                        [(nth (get index (nth row 2)) 3)])\n  1044\t                (map second places))))\n  1045\t          (walk\n  1046\t            [store a]\n  1047\t            (let [row (get index a)\n  1048\t                  store (cond\n  1049\t                          (= standin-tag (row-tag row))\n  1050\t                          (let [[_ _ nm k] row\n  1051\t                                entry (get catalogue k)]\n  1052\t                            (if (and entry (= nm (:name entry)))\n  1053\t                              (assoc store nm\n  1054\t                                     (macro-entry (:macro-tree entry)\n  1055\t                                                  vm/ast-contract))\n  1056\t                              store))\n  1057\t\n  1058\t                          :else\n  1059\t                          (if-let [{:keys [name]} (definition-at index a)]\n  1060\t                            (dissoc store name)\n  1061\t                            store))]\n  1062\t              (reduce walk store (children row))))]\n  1063\t    (walk store root)))\n  1064\t\n  1065\t\n  1066\t;; =============================================================================\n  1067\t;; Events (§8)\n  1068\t;; =============================================================================\n  1069\t\n  1070\t(defn- event-row\n  1071\t  \"The expansion record (§8). `correspondence` — nil for a failed\n  1072\t   attempt — is the per-occurrence correspondence of the successful\n  1073\t   output (ruling U1): `{path :constructed | [:retained origin]}` for\n  1074\t   every `:application` occurrence of the output, at its path relative\n  1075\t   to the output root, read from the construction history the macro's\n  1076\t   own code threaded through the packets it built. A `:constructed`\n  1077\t   occurrence names THIS record as its generating event (the record it\n  1078\t   is retained in); a `[:retained origin]` occurrence