{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1795310000000-owner-ruling-occurrence-identity-unitarity.md; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '565,850p'\"","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-11-08 2x:xx +0700\nCoding-Agent: interactive (ZCode, yang.clojure orchestrator seat)\nStatus: DRAFT — pending owner sign-off (ruling text from the owner's words in session; filed verbatim-in-substance below)\n\n# OWNER RULING OF RECORD — occurrence identity under unitarity (resolves the codex cc1 gate reject)\n\n## The owner's principle (quoted-in-substance)\n\nThe compilation pipeline is transformation of values over dao.stream, so unitarity applies: **information is never lost**. The mapping is **bijective** — two things may compile to the same thing and should have the same content hash, but because of unitarity, **the complete history of the transformation is intact**. Two things may compile to the same thing and have the same hash **but have different history that can be recovered**.\n\n## Rulings derived (U1–U3)\n\n**U1 — an occurrence is not its content address.** The occurrence identity is **(content address, origin)** — the address as reached through a specific transformation event. \"Two occurrences of identical content\" is well-formed: they differ in history, not content. The per-occurrence origins in the call-site side table, keyed on `[origin root-address path]`, ARE the query that recovers the distinction (design §2.1/§2.3). Codex's P1-a objection (\"identical generated/input applications share an address, so provenance cannot be classified by content\") is ANSWERED: provenance is not classified by content — it is read from the retained history: the expansion-event record behind a `[:expansion record-address]` origin, the source position behind a `[:source …]` origin. Never minted, never guessed from content.\n\n**U2 — admission identity is history-recoverable, declared by the composition.** If the composition's history contains two admission events, bijectivity demands both are recoverable — collapsing them into one deterministic token loses information and violates unitarity. If the history contains one event, minting a fresh token fabricates history — the violation in the other direction. Only the composition knows which its history contains, so the composition DECLARES the distinction when it exists (the caller-owned admission scope / explicit `:yin.link.publish/admission` token), and the deterministic content-derived default is CORRECT precisely because re-publication of identical content with no declared distinction IS one event. Codex's P1-b objection is ANSWERED on these grounds: the requirement is not \"every admission mints a fresh token\" (that fabricates history) but \"every DISTINCT event is representable and recoverable\" (the scoped/explicit mechanism provides it; the composition supplies it when its history contains two events).\n\n**U3 — the general principle.** Identity is never minted from structure OR from process. Occurrence distinctness is either (i) READ from retained history (per-occurrence origins, expansion events), or (ii) DECLARED by the party whose history it is (composition-supplied admission identities). Provenance remains recoverable by address or query over datoms — axiom 2 holds in both channels.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- The cc1 branch state (d91489f7) STANDS as the implementation of U1/U2 — no further design-level code change is required to answer the codex reject; the objection is resolved on the record by this ruling.\n- The landing sequence proceeds: astra re-check against this ruling → codex re-gate → merge to master → the exception track's R3 dispatch → adoption rounds 2–4 + D1.\n- Addendum A's occurrence contract is unaffected in shape: K = [origin root-address path], `:yang/call-site 1`, the occurrence/content boundary — all unchanged. U1 clarifies WHAT an origin identifies (an event in the retained history), not how it attaches.\n\n— drafted by the yang.clojure orchestrator seat from the owner's ruling in session\n   565\t\n   566\t(defn- throw-prelude\n   567\t  [msg data]\n   568\t  (throw (ex-info msg (assoc data :yin.macro/prelude true))))\n   569\t\n   570\t\n   571\t(defn- packet?\n   572\t  [x]\n   573\t  (and (vector? x) (= 2 (count x)) (jing/segment-address? (first x))\n   574\t       (vector? (second x))))\n   575\t\n   576\t\n   577\t(defn- need-packet\n   578\t  [who x]\n   579\t  (when-not (packet? x)\n   580\t    (throw-prelude (str who \" expects a tree packet\") {:op who}))\n   581\t  x)\n   582\t\n   583\t\n   584\t(defn- merge-packets\n   585\t  \"Union the rows of `packets` into one index, verifying that one address\n   586\t   denotes one body (§5.3).\"\n   587\t  [packets]\n   588\t  (reduce (fn [index row]\n   589\t            (let [prior (get index (first row))]\n   590\t              (cond (nil? prior) (assoc index (first row) row)\n   591\t                    (same-value? prior row) index\n   592\t                    :else (throw-prelude \"Packet address conflict\"\n   593\t                                         {:address (first row)}))))\n   594\t          {}\n   595\t          (mapcat second packets)))\n   596\t\n   597\t\n   598\t(def ^:private pending-expansion-origin\n   599\t  \"The construction origin the prelude attaches to every node the\n   600\t   macro's code builds during one invocation (ruling U1: identity comes\n   601\t   from the construction event, never from comparing content\n   602\t   addresses). `expand-call` substitutes the recorded expansion event's\n   603\t   `[:expansion record-address]` origin for it when the output's\n   604\t   occurrence correspondence is read — the placeholder never reaches a\n   605\t   table, a row, or an event it does not belong to.\"\n   606\t  [:expansion ::pending])\n   607\t\n   608\t\n   609\t(defn- with-origin-of\n   610\t  \"Tag packet `p` with `f`, its construction origin function: `(f rel)`\n   611\t   answers the origin of the occurrence at `rel`, a path relative to\n   612\t   `p`'s root — the pending expansion origin for a node the macro's\n   613\t   code constructed, or, below a child coordinate that retains a\n   614\t   passed-through packet, that packet's own origin function. The\n   615\t   function rides the packet's metadata, so it is content-addressing\n   616\t   invisible and never leaks into a final tree.\"\n   617\t  [p f]\n   618\t  (vary-meta p assoc ::origin-of f))\n   619\t\n   620\t\n   621\t(defn- origin-of-fn\n   622\t  \"The construction origin function packet `p` carries, or nil.\"\n   623\t  [p]\n   624\t  (::origin-of (meta p)))\n   625\t\n   626\t\n   627\t(defn- constructed-origin-fn\n   628\t  \"The origin function of a packet the prelude constructed: its root\n   629\t   occurrence carries the pending expansion origin; a relative path\n   630\t   below a child coordinate delegates to the packet passed for that\n   631\t   child — a spliced operand retains its own incoming origin, however\n   632\t   the macro's code embedded it.\"\n   633\t  [coord-children]\n   634\t  (fn [rel]\n   635\t    (if (empty? rel)\n   636\t      pending-expansion-origin\n   637\t      (if-some [child (get coord-children (first rel))]\n   638\t        (if-some [f (origin-of-fn child)]\n   639\t          (f (subvec rel 1))\n   640\t          pending-expansion-origin)\n   641\t        pending-expansion-origin))))\n   642\t\n   643\t\n   644\t(defn- construct\n   645\t  \"Intern `body` over the rows of its child `packets`; a closed packet.\n   646\t   Every node interned here is CONSTRUCTED by the expansion's code\n   647\t   (ruling U1), so the result packet carries the construction origin\n   648\t   function and the output's per-occurrence origins are read from this\n   649\t   construction history — never inferred by comparing content\n   650\t   addresses: a constructed node whose content equals a retained\n   651\t   node's stays distinct, because its origin answers through this\n   652\t   function and not through its address.\"\n   653\t  [body packets]\n   654\t  (let [index (merge-packets packets)\n   655\t        [index a] (intern-body index body)\n   656\t        coord-children (into {}\n   657\t                             (map (fn [[place p]] [(first place) p]))\n   658\t                             (map vector (child-places (get index a)) packets))]\n   659\t    (with-origin-of (packet-of index a) (constructed-origin-fn coord-children))))\n   660\t\n   661\t\n   662\t(defn- root-row\n   663\t  [[root rows]]\n   664\t  (some #(when (= root (first %)) %) rows))\n   665\t\n   666\t\n   667\t(defn- literal-packet\n   668\t  [v]\n   669\t  (construct [:literal v] []))\n   670\t\n   671\t\n   672\t(defn- application-packet\n   673\t  [operator operands]\n   674\t  (construct [:application (first operator) (mapv first operands) false]\n   675\t             (cons operator operands)))\n   676\t\n   677\t\n   678\t(defn- lambda-packet\n   679\t  [params body]\n   680\t  (when-not (and (sequential? params) (every? symbol? params))\n   681\t    (throw-prelude \"yin/lambda params must be symbols\" {:op 'yin/lambda}))\n   682\t  (construct [:lambda (vec params) (first body)] [body]))\n   683\t\n   684\t\n   685\t(defn- name-of\n   686\t  [tree]\n   687\t  (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/name-of tree))\n   688\t        v (nth row 2 nil)]\n   689\t    (cond (= :variable (row-tag row)) v\n   690\t          (and (= :literal (row-tag row)) (symbol? v)) v\n   691\t          (and (= :literal (row-tag row)) (string? v)) (symbol v)\n   692\t          :else (throw-prelude \"yin/name-of reads a variable, literal symbol, or literal string\"\n   693\t                               {:op 'yin/name-of}))))\n   694\t\n   695\t\n   696\t(defn- sequence-body\n   697\t  \"The reference `do` lowering: `(do a b c)` is `((fn [_] ((fn [_] c) b)) a)`;\n   698\t   one form is itself and none is the literal nil.\"\n   699\t  [trees]\n   700\t  (let [trees (vec trees)]\n   701\t    (doseq [t trees] (need-packet 'yin/sequence-body t))\n   702\t    (case (count trees)\n   703\t      0 (literal-packet nil)\n   704\t      1 (first trees)\n   705\t      (application-packet (lambda-packet ['_] (sequence-body (subvec trees 1)))\n   706\t                          [(first trees)]))))\n   707\t\n   708\t\n   709\t(defn- slot-of\n   710\t  [tree n]\n   711\t  (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/slot tree))\n   712\t        kinds (into {} (slot-kinds (row-tag row)))\n   713\t        index (packet-index tree)\n   714\t        ;; an extracted slot is input syntax READ, not built: the\n   715\t        ;; extracted packet retains the source packet's construction\n   716\t        ;; origin function, descending through the slot's coordinate\n   717\t        ofn (or (origin-of-fn tree)\n   718\t                (fn [_] pending-expansion-origin))]\n   719\t    (when-not (and (integer? n) (contains? kinds n))\n   720\t      (throw-prelude \"yin/slot position names no grammar slot\"\n   721\t                     {:op 'yin/slot, :position n}))\n   722\t    (case (get kinds n)\n   723\t      :node (with-origin-of (packet-of index (nth row n))\n   724\t              (fn [rel] (ofn (into [n] rel))))\n   725\t      :nodes (map-indexed (fn [i c]\n   726\t                            (with-origin-of (packet-of index c)\n   727\t                              (fn [rel] (ofn (into [[n i]] rel)))))\n   728\t                          (nth row n))\n   729\t      (nth row n))))\n   730\t\n   731\t\n   732\t(defn prelude\n   733\t  \"The closed body environment (§5.3): the pure standard primitives (no\n   734\t   `require`, no stream or FFI constructor) and the row-native constructors,\n   735\t   each consuming and returning self-contained tree packets. `gensym` is the\n   736\t   invocation-local `yin/gensym-sym`.\"\n   737\t  [gensym]\n   738\t  (merge\n   739\t    (dissoc vm/primitives 'require 'try-require 'bytes->str)\n   740\t    {'yin/tag (fn [tree] (row-tag (root-row (need-packet 'yin/tag tree)))),\n   741\t     'yin/slot slot-of,\n   742\t     'yin/literal literal-packet,\n   743\t     'yin/variable (fn [sym]\n   744\t                     (when-not (symbol? sym)\n   745\t                       (throw-prelude \"yin/variable expects a symbol\" {:op 'yin/variable}))\n   746\t                     (construct [:variable sym] [])),\n   747\t     'yin/lambda (fn [params body] (lambda-packet params (need-packet 'yin/lambda body))),\n   748\t     'yin/application (fn [operator operands]\n   749\t                        (need-packet 'yin/application operator)\n   750\t                        (doseq [o operands] (need-packet 'yin/application o))\n   751\t                        (application-packet operator (vec operands))),\n   752\t     'yin/if (fn [t c a]\n   753\t               (doseq [x [t c a]] (need-packet 'yin/if x))\n   754\t               (construct [:if (first t) (first c) (first a)] [t c a])),\n   755\t     'yin/sequence-body sequence-body,\n   756\t     'yin/make-lambda (fn [params-tree body]\n   757\t                        (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/make-lambda params-tree))]\n   758\t                          (when-not (and (= :literal (row-tag row))\n   759\t                                         (vector? (nth row 2))\n   760\t                                         (every? symbol? (nth row 2)))\n   761\t                            (throw-prelude \"yin/make-lambda reads a literal parameter vector\"\n   762\t                                           {:op 'yin/make-lambda}))\n   763\t                          (lambda-packet (nth row 2) (need-packet 'yin/make-lambda body)))),\n   764\t     'yin/make-def (fn [name-tree value-tree]\n   765\t                     (application-packet (construct [:variable 'yin/def] [])\n   766\t                                         [(literal-packet (name-of name-tree))\n   767\t                                          (need-packet 'yin/make-def value-tree)])),\n   768\t     'yin/name-of name-of,\n   769\t     'yin/gensym-sym gensym}))\n   770\t\n   771\t\n   772\t(def ^:private suspending-tags\n   773\t  #{:vm/park :vm/resume :dao.stream.apply/call})\n   774\t\n   775\t\n   776\t(def ^:private effect-tags\n   777\t  #{:stream/make :stream/put :stream/cursor :stream/next :stream/close})\n   778\t\n   779\t\n   780\t(defn- catch-message\n   781\t  [e]\n   782\t  (or (ex-message e) (str e)))\n   783\t\n   784\t\n   785\t(defn bounded-row-evaluator\n   786\t  \"The default body runner (§5.2): a fresh throwaway ast-walker loaded from\n   787\t   the lambda body's rows, its parameters bound in `env`, the closed\n   788\t   `prelude` as its only primitives, no store, no module resolver, no stream\n   789\t   constructor, and no FFI bridge. It counts VM transitions.\n   790\t\n   791\t   Returns `{:value v}`, or `{:error e}` with `e` one of\n   792\t   `{:kind :fuel-guard :steps n}`, `{:kind :suspended}` (a park, resume,\n   793\t   bridge call, blocked read, or work scheduled outside the body\n   794\t   continuation), `{:kind :effect-guard :tag t}` (a stream constructor), or\n   795\t   `{:kind :body-error :message s}` (the body threw).\n   796\t\n   797\t   `contract` is the packet's own AST stamp, carried from its store entry\n   798\t   by `invoke`, which has verified it; the body rows load under that stamp,\n   799\t   never one this runner supplies, and a missing or old stamp is refused\n   800\t   (thrown) before anything runs.\"\n   801\t  [{:keys [macro-tree contract env prelude max-steps]}]\n   802\t  (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract contract)\n   803\t  (let [index (packet-index macro-tree)\n   804\t        body (nth (get index (first macro-tree)) 3)\n   805\t        body-set {:root body, :rows (into {} (map (fn [a] [a (get index a)]))\n   806\t                                          (reachable index body))}]\n   807\t    (try\n   808\t      (loop [v (ast-walker/vm-load-rows\n   809\t                 (ast-walker/create-vm {:env env, :primitives prelude,\n   810\t                                        :primitive-profiles {}})\n   811\t                 body-set\n   812\t                 contract)\n   813\t             steps 0]\n   814\t        (let [tag (:type (:control v))]\n   815\t          (cond (or (:blocked? v) (seq (:wait-set v)) (seq (:parked v)))\n   816\t                {:error {:kind :suspended}}\n   817\t\n   818\t                (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? v) {:value (:value v)}\n   819\t\n   820\t                (:halted? v) {:error {:kind :suspended}}\n   821\t\n   822\t                (>= steps max-steps) {:error {:kind :fuel-guard, :steps steps}}\n   823\t\n   824\t                (contains? suspending-tags tag) {:error {:kind :suspended}}\n   825\t\n   826\t                (contains? effect-tags tag) {:error {:kind :effect-guard, :tag tag}}\n   827\t\n   828\t                :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc steps)))))\n   829\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   830\t        {:error {:kind :body-error, :message (catch-message e)}}))))\n   831\t\n   832\t\n   833\t(defn- bind-arguments\n   834\t  \"Positional binding of operand packets to lambda parameters; `[a & rest]`\n   835\t   binds `rest` to the vector of remaining packets. `{:env m}` or\n   836\t   `{:expected n :got m}`.\"\n   837\t  [params args]\n   838\t  (let [[fixed [amp rest-sym]] (split-with #(not= '& %) params)\n   839\t        fixed (vec fixed)\n   840\t        n (count fixed)\n   841\t        m (count args)]\n   842\t    (if amp\n   843\t      (if (< m n)\n   844\t        {:expected n, :got m}\n   845\t        {:env (assoc (zipmap fixed args) rest-sym (vec (drop n args)))})\n   846\t      (if (not= m n)\n   847\t        {:expected n, :got m}\n   848\t        {:env (zipmap fixed args)}))))\n   849\t\n   850\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
