{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '850,935p;1060,1515p'\"","aggregated_output":"   850\t\n   851\t(defn- attempt-id\n   852\t  [ctx counter]\n   853\t  [(get-in ctx [:incarnation :yin.expander/token]) counter])\n   854\t\n   855\t\n   856\t(defn macro-entry\n   857\t  \"A macro-store value: a self-contained lambda tree `packet` with the AST\n   858\t   `contract` it was produced under. The store holds only these. The\n   859\t   transformer runner verifies the contract before it executes the packet\n   860\t   (Rule R: a persistent or supplied code packet is never relabelled), and\n   861\t   the expander stamps only what it harvests itself, under\n   862\t   `vm/ast-contract`.\"\n   863\t  [packet contract]\n   864\t  {:yin.macro/tree packet, :yin.macro/contract contract})\n   865\t\n   866\t\n   867\t(defn- verified-tree\n   868\t  \"The packet of a macro-store value after its contract is verified\n   869\t   against `vm/ast-contract`: `:contract-missing` for a bare packet or an\n   870\t   entry without one, `:contract-mismatch` for an old stamp.\"\n   871\t  [entry]\n   872\t  (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract\n   873\t                      (when (map? entry) (:yin.macro/contract entry)))\n   874\t  (:yin.macro/tree entry))\n   875\t\n   876\t\n   877\t(defn- check-store!\n   878\t  \"A supplied macro store: no reserved name is a macro (Rule R), and every\n   879\t   entry carries the current AST contract. Returns `store`.\"\n   880\t  [store]\n   881\t  (vm/check-bindings! :macro store)\n   882\t  (doseq [entry (vals store)] (verified-tree entry))\n   883\t  store)\n   884\t\n   885\t\n   886\t(defn- invoke*\n   887\t  \"Run one macro body. `entry` is a macro-store value (`macro-entry`),\n   888\t   verified before anything runs. `counter` is the attempt counter, which\n   889\t   gensyms read. `{:tree packet}` or `{:error e}`.\"\n   890\t  [entry operands ctx counter]\n   891\t  (let [macro-tree (verified-tree entry)\n   892\t        macro-root (first macro-tree)\n   893\t        params (nth (root-row macro-tree) 2)\n   894\t        {:keys [env expected got]} (bind-arguments params operands)]\n   895\t    (if-not env\n   896\t      {:error {:kind :arity, :macro macro-root, :expected expected, :got got}}\n   897\t      (let [n (volatile! 0)\n   898\t            token (get-in ctx [:incarnation :yin.expander/token])\n   899\t            gensym (fn [prefix]\n   900\t                     (let [i @n]\n   901\t                       (vswap! n inc)\n   902\t                       (symbol (str (if (symbol? prefix) (name prefix) prefix)\n   903\t                                    \"__\" token \"_\" counter \"_\" i))))\n   904\t            run (or (:eval ctx) bounded-row-evaluator)\n   905\t            {:keys [value error]} (run {:macro-tree macro-tree,\n   906\t                                        :contract (:yin.macro/contract entry),\n   907\t                                        :env env,\n   908\t                                        :prelude (prelude gensym),\n   909\t                                        :max-steps (get-in ctx [:guards :max-steps])})]\n   910\t        (if error\n   911\t          {:error (assoc error :macro macro-root)}\n   912\t          {:tree value})))))\n   913\t\n   914\t\n   915\t(def default-guards\n   916\t  {:max-depth 100,\n   917\t   :max-rows-per-expansion 10000,\n   918\t   :max-rows-per-batch nil,\n   919\t   :max-steps 100000})\n   920\t\n   921\t\n   922\t(defn invoke\n   923\t  \"Run `entry`, a macro-store value (`macro-entry`: a self-contained lambda\n   924\t   packet and its AST contract), on `operand-trees` and return its result\n   925\t   tree packet, unvalidated. The contract is verified first\n   926\t   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`, thrown). Gensyms use\n   927\t   `(:attempt ctx)` as the attempt counter. Throws `ex-info` carrying the\n   928\t   error data on an arity, guard, suspension, or body failure.\"\n   929\t  [entry operand-trees ctx]\n   930\t  (let [ctx (update ctx :guards #(merge default-guards %))\n   931\t        {:keys [tree error]} (invoke* entry (vec operand-trees) ctx\n   932\t                                      (:attempt ctx))]\n   933\t    (when error\n   934\t      (throw (ex-info \"Macro invocation failed\" error)))\n   935\t    tree))\n  1060\t                            (dissoc store name)\n  1061\t                            store))]\n  1062\t              (reduce walk store (children row))))]\n  1063\t    (walk store root)))\n  1064\t\n  1065\t\n  1066\t;; =============================================================================\n  1067\t;; Events (§8)\n  1068\t;; =============================================================================\n  1069\t\n  1070\t(defn- event-row\n  1071\t  \"The expansion record (§8). `correspondence` — nil for a failed\n  1072\t   attempt — is the per-occurrence correspondence of the successful\n  1073\t   output (ruling U1): `{path :constructed | [:retained origin]}` for\n  1074\t   every `:application` occurrence of the output, at its path relative\n  1075\t   to the output root, read from the construction history the macro's\n  1076\t   own code threaded through the packets it built. A `:constructed`\n  1077\t   occurrence names THIS record as its generating event (the record it\n  1078\t   is retained in); a `[:retained origin]` occurrence names the\n  1079\t   incoming origin its syntax already carried. The call-site side\n  1080\t   table derives each marked occurrence's origin from this record.\"\n  1081\t  [attempt source-batch origin parent input-root call-path macro-root output-root\n  1082\t   error correspondence]\n  1083\t  (intern-row [:yin.macro/expand attempt source-batch origin parent input-root\n  1084\t               call-path macro-root output-root error correspondence]))\n  1085\t\n  1086\t\n  1087\t(defn- source-origin\n  1088\t  [ctx source-batch tree-index]\n  1089\t  [:source (:source-medium ctx) source-batch tree-index])\n  1090\t\n  1091\t\n  1092\t;; =============================================================================\n  1093\t;; Expansion (§4)\n  1094\t;; =============================================================================\n  1095\t\n  1096\t(defn- fail\n  1097\t  [st error]\n  1098\t  (assoc st :error error))\n  1099\t\n  1100\t\n  1101\t(defn- allocate-attempt\n  1102\t  [st]\n  1103\t  (let [counter (get-in st [:ctx :attempt])]\n  1104\t    [(update-in st [:ctx :attempt] inc) counter]))\n  1105\t\n  1106\t\n  1107\t(defn- macro-of\n  1108\t  \"The stored macro packet for an operator occurrence: a `:variable` naming\n  1109\t   a store entry that no enclosing lambda parameter shadows.\"\n  1110\t  [st operator shadow]\n  1111\t  (let [row (get (:index st) operator)]\n  1112\t    (when (and (= :variable (row-tag row))\n  1113\t               (not (contains? shadow (nth row 2))))\n  1114\t      (get (:store st) (nth row 2)))))\n  1115\t\n  1116\t\n  1117\t(defn- record-event\n  1118\t  [st event-row*]\n  1119\t  (update st :events conj event-row*))\n  1120\t\n  1121\t\n  1122\t(defn- guard-batch-rows\n  1123\t  [st]\n  1124\t  (let [limit (get-in st [:ctx :guards :max-rows-per-batch])\n  1125\t        n (count (:index st))]\n  1126\t    (when (and limit (> n limit))\n  1127\t      {:kind :row-guard, :scope :batch, :rows n})))\n  1128\t\n  1129\t\n  1130\t(defn- merge-output\n  1131\t  \"Merge a validated result packet into the working index; an address whose\n  1132\t   working body differs is an `:address-conflict`.\"\n  1133\t  [st [_ rows]]\n  1134\t  (reduce (fn [st row]\n  1135\t            (let [prior (get (:index st) (first row))]\n  1136\t              (cond (nil? prior) (assoc-in st [:index (first row)] row)\n  1137\t                    (same-value? prior row) st\n  1138\t                    :else (reduced (assoc st ::conflict (first row))))))\n  1139\t          st\n  1140\t          rows))\n  1141\t\n  1142\t\n  1143\t(declare expand-node)\n  1144\t\n  1145\t\n  1146\t(defn- output-correspondence\n  1147\t  \"The per-occurrence correspondence of the expansion's output (ruling\n  1148\t   U1): for every `:application` occurrence of output packet `tree`, at\n  1149\t   its path relative to the output root, `:constructed` when the\n  1150\t   expansion's code built that node, or `[:retained origin]` when the\n  1151\t   node is input syntax retained with its own incoming origin. The\n  1152\t   classification is the construction origin function the prelude\n  1153\t   threaded through the packets the macro's code built — never a\n  1154\t   comparison of content addresses; the recorded expansion event\n  1155\t   retains the answer, and the site table derives each marked\n  1156\t   occurrence's origin from it.\"\n  1157\t  [tree ofn]\n  1158\t  (into {}\n  1159\t        (map (fn [path]\n  1160\t               (let [o (ofn path)]\n  1161\t                 [path (if (= pending-expansion-origin o)\n  1162\t                         :constructed\n  1163\t                         [:retained o])])))\n  1164\t        (sort-by pr-str\n  1165\t                 (map second\n  1166\t                      (vm/application-occurrences (packet->row-set tree))))))\n  1167\t\n  1168\t\n  1169\t(defn- expand-call\n  1170\t  \"One recognized call: allocate an attempt, begin its event before any\n  1171\t   guard or invocation, run the transformer on the operand packets, validate\n  1172\t   and merge the result, finish the event, and reconsider the result at the\n  1173\t   same occurrence with depth + 1.\n  1174\t\n  1175\t   Each operand packet enters the invocation carrying its occurrence\n  1176\t   origin function — the enclosing walk's origin at the operand's own\n  1177\t   absolute path — and the prelude threads it through every node the\n  1178\t   macro's code constructs (ruling U1): a spliced operand retains its\n  1179\t   own incoming origin, a built node carries the pending expansion\n  1180\t   origin. The output's per-occurrence correspondence is read from that\n  1181\t   construction history, retained in the event record, and the\n  1182\t   recursive walk answers origins from the record — never from\n  1183\t   comparing content addresses.\"\n  1184\t  [st address entry {:keys [path rel frame shadow depth origin-of]}]\n  1185\t  (let [[st counter] (allocate-attempt st)\n  1186\t        ctx (:ctx st)\n  1187\t        macro-root (first (:yin.macro/tree entry))\n  1188\t        begin (fn [output error correspondence]\n  1189\t                (event-row (attempt-id ctx counter)\n  1190\t                           (:source-batch st)\n  1191\t                           (when-not (:parent frame)\n  1192\t                             (source-origin ctx (:source-batch st) (:tree-index frame)))\n  1193\t                           (:parent frame)\n  1194\t                           (:root frame)\n  1195\t                           rel\n  1196\t                           macro-root\n  1197\t                           output\n  1198\t                           error\n  1199\t                           correspondence))\n  1200\t        failed (fn [st error]\n  1201\t                 (-> st (record-event (begin nil error nil)) (fail error)))\n  1202\t        guards (:guards ctx)]\n  1203\t    (if (>= depth (:max-depth guards))\n  1204\t      [(failed st {:kind :depth-guard, :depth depth, :path path}) address]\n  1205\t      (let [row (get (:index st) address)\n  1206\t            operands (map-indexed\n  1207\t                      (fn [i a]\n  1208\t                        (with-origin-of (packet-of (:index st) a)\n  1209\t                          (fn [rel]\n  1210\t                            (origin-of (into (conj path [3 i]) rel)))))\n  1211\t                      (nth row 3))\n  1212\t            {:keys [tree error]} (invoke* entry operands ctx counter)\n  1213\t            invalid (fn [reason]\n  1214\t                      {:kind :invalid-output, :macro macro-root, :path path,\n  1215\t                       :reason reason})]\n  1216\t        (if error\n  1217\t          [(failed st error) address]\n  1218\t          (if-let [e (valid-tree? tree {:working? true})]\n  1219\t            [(failed st (invalid (:reason e))) address]\n  1220\t            (let [n (count (set (map first (second tree))))]\n  1221\t              (if (> n (:max-rows-per-expansion guards))\n  1222\t                [(failed st {:kind :row-guard, :scope :expansion, :rows n}) address]\n  1223\t                (let [st' (merge-output st tree)]\n  1224\t                  (if (::conflict st')\n  1225\t                    [(failed st (invalid :address-conflict)) address]\n  1226\t                    (if-let [e (guard-batch-rows st')]\n  1227\t                      [(failed st' e) address]\n  1228\t                      (let [;; the output's construction origin function\n  1229\t                            ;; (ruling U1); an output the prelude did not\n  1230\t                            ;; thread — unreachable through the sanctioned\n  1231\t                            ;; constructors — classifies as constructed\n  1232\t                            ofn (or (origin-of-fn tree)\n  1233\t                                    (fn [_] pending-expansion-origin))\n  1234\t                            corr (output-correspondence tree ofn)\n  1235\t                            out (first tree)\n  1236\t                            ev (begin out nil corr)\n  1237\t                            st' (-> st'\n  1238\t                                    (record-event ev)\n  1239\t                                    (update :produced\n  1240\t                                            (fn [p]\n  1241\t                                              (if (some #(= out (first %)) p)\n  1242\t                                                p\n  1243\t                                                (conj p (packet-of (:index st') out))))))]\n  1244\t                        (expand-node st' out\n  1245\t                                     {:path path,\n  1246\t                                      :rel [],\n  1247\t                                      :frame {:parent (first ev), :root out},\n  1248\t                                      :shadow shadow,\n  1249\t                                      :depth (inc depth),\n  1250\t                                      ;; per-occurrence origins read from\n  1251\t                                      ;; the RETAINED correspondence (§2.1,\n  1252\t                                      ;; §8): a `[:retained origin]` names\n  1253\t                                      ;; the incoming origin the syntax\n  1254\t                                      ;; already carried, a `:constructed`\n  1255\t                                      ;; occurrence names the recorded\n  1256\t                                      ;; expansion event — the record the\n  1257\t                                      ;; correspondence is retained in\n  1258\t                                      :origin-of\n  1259\t                                      (fn [abs-path]\n  1260\t                                        (let [o (get corr (subvec abs-path (count path)))]\n  1261\t                                          (if (and (vector? o) (= :retained (first o)))\n  1262\t                                            (second o)\n  1263\t                                            [:expansion (first ev)])))})))))))))))))\n  1264\t\n  1265\t\n  1266\t(defn- expand-children\n  1267\t  \"Expand `row`'s children in order `places` under per-child shadows;\n  1268\t   `[st address']`, rebuilding the row when any child changed.\"\n  1269\t  [st row places shadow-of {:keys [path rel] :as loc}]\n  1270\t  (let [[st children']\n  1271\t        (reduce (fn [[st acc] [coord c]]\n  1272\t                  (if (:error st)\n  1273\t                    (reduced [st acc])\n  1274\t                    (let [[st c'] (expand-node st c\n  1275\t                                               (assoc loc\n  1276\t                                                      :path (conj path coord)\n  1277\t                                                      :rel (conj rel coord)\n  1278\t                                                      :shadow (shadow-of coord)))]\n  1279\t                      [st (conj acc c')])))\n  1280\t                [st []]\n  1281\t                places)]\n  1282\t    (if (:error st)\n  1283\t      [st (first row)]\n  1284\t      (let [[index a'] (rebuild-row (:index st) row places children')]\n  1285\t        [(assoc st :index index) a']))))\n  1286\t\n  1287\t\n  1288\t(defn- expand-node\n  1289\t  \"§4.2. `loc` carries the absolute `path` in the batch's run tree, the\n  1290\t   `rel` path within the current `frame` (`{:root r :parent event|nil\n  1291\t   :tree-index j}`), the lexical `shadow` set, the expansion `depth`,\n  1292\t   and `:origin-of` — the occurrence-provenance function of §2.1, which\n  1293\t   answers, for an ABSOLUTE occurrence path, the origin of the\n  1294\t   admission or generation event that produced the syntax there.\n  1295\t   Every application\n  1296\t   occurrence is recorded under its absolute path as it is visited, so\n  1297\t   the finalizer can name each occurrence's real origin; an occurrence\n  1298\t   replaced by an expansion is re-recorded by the expansion's own walk,\n  1299\t   and a stale entry for a path the finished tree no longer applies at\n  1300\t   is simply never read. Returns `[st address']`; a failure sets\n  1301\t   `(:error st)`.\"\n  1302\t  [st address {:keys [shadow] :as loc}]\n  1303\t  (if (:error st)\n  1304\t    [st address]\n  1305\t    (let [row (get (:index st) address)\n  1306\t          tag (row-tag row)]\n  1307\t      (cond\n  1308\t        (and (= :application tag) (macro-of st (nth row 2) shadow))\n  1309\t        (expand-call st address (macro-of st (nth row 2) shadow) loc)\n  1310\t\n  1311\t        (= :application tag)\n  1312\t        (let [st (update-in st [:call-site-origins]\n  1313\t                            assoc (:path loc) ((:origin-of loc) (:path loc)))\n  1314\t              op (nth row 2)\n  1315\t              [st op'] (expand-node st op (-> loc\n  1316\t                                              (update :path conj 2)\n  1317\t                                              (update :rel conj 2)))]\n  1318\t          (if (:error st)\n  1319\t            [st address]\n  1320\t            (let [[index app'] (if (= op op')\n  1321\t                                 [(:index st) address]\n  1322\t                                 (intern-body (:index st) (assoc (subvec row 1) 1 op')))\n  1323\t                  st (assoc st :index index)\n  1324\t                  row' (get index app')]\n  1325\t              (if (macro-of st op' shadow)\n  1326\t                ;; recognition is not expansion: depth is unchanged\n  1327\t                (expand-node st app' loc)\n  1328\t                (expand-children st row' (rest (child-places row'))\n  1329\t                                 (constantly shadow) loc)))))\n  1330\t\n  1331\t        :else\n  1332\t        (let [shadow' (if (= :lambda tag) (into shadow (nth row 2)) shadow)]\n  1333\t          (expand-children st row (child-places row)\n  1334\t                           (constantly shadow') loc))))))\n  1335\t\n  1336\t\n  1337\t;; =============================================================================\n  1338\t;; The batch (§3.1, §3.2)\n  1339\t;; =============================================================================\n  1340\t\n  1341\t(defn- log-packet\n  1342\t  [st]\n  1343\t  [:yin.macro/log (:events st) (:produced st)])\n  1344\t\n  1345\t\n  1346\t(defn- with-default-guards\n  1347\t  [ctx]\n  1348\t  (update ctx :guards #(merge default-guards %)))\n  1349\t\n  1350\t\n  1351\t(defn- batch-call-site-claims\n  1352\t  \"The per-member call-site (C1) claim verdicts the encoder recorded on\n  1353\t   `batch`: nil when no member claimed coverage, otherwise one boolean\n  1354\t   per member — the encoder validated every member's markers against\n  1355\t   its own tree at the boundary, so a member whose markers do not\n  1356\t   exactly cover it was refused there, never delivered here. Each\n  1357\t   member's own verdict decides its metadata: only a member that\n  1358\t   claimed coverage finalizes a side table, whatever its siblings\n  1359\t   claimed.\"\n  1360\t  [batch]\n  1361\t  (nth batch 5 nil))\n  1362\t\n  1363\t\n  1364\t(defn- final-call-site-metadata\n  1365\t  \"The call-site occurrence contract's (C1) side table of an expanded\n  1366\t   final tree, as frontend-metadata rows `[origin root path\n  1367\t   :yang/call-site 1]` in printed-row order: one row per\n  1368\t   `:application` occurrence of the stand-in-lowered, tail-marked tree\n  1369\t   that actually executes. The frontend's own markers named the\n  1370\t   pre-expansion tree; expansion, tail marking and stand-in lowering\n  1371\t   recompute roots and paths, so no pre-expansion table can cover this\n  1372\t   tree and the table is finalized here, over the finished rows.\n  1373\t\n  1374\t   Each row's origin is that occurrence's REAL origin (design §2.1,\n  1375\t   §2.3): `occurrence-origins` maps the final occurrence path to the\n  1376\t   origin of the admission or generation event that produced the\n  1377\t   application syntax at that path — the admitted run member's source\n  1378\t   origin for retained syntax (a no-op expansion keeps it valid), and\n  1379\t   the `[:expansion record-address]` of the recorded expansion event\n  1380\t   whose output introduced generated syntax. No expansion-record\n  1381\t   address is fabricated: only event rows the expander actually\n  1382\t   recorded appear. The table is therefore the explicit\n  1383\t   final-root correspondence §2.3 requires — every generated occurrence\n  1384\t   names its producing record, so an attribution consumer can reach the\n  1385\t   event (its input root, call path, macro root, output root) from the\n  1386\t   row alone.\"\n  1387\t  [row-set occurrence-origins admission-origin]\n  1388\t  (vec (sort-by pr-str\n  1389\t                (map (fn [[root path]]\n  1390\t                       [(get occurrence-origins path admission-origin)\n  1391\t                        root path :yang/call-site 1])\n  1392\t                     (vm/application-occurrences row-set)))))\n  1393\t\n  1394\t\n  1395\t(defn expand-batch\n  1396\t  \"Expand one input batch against `ctx` (§3.2). Returns\n  1397\t   `{:status :ok :tree packet :log log :ctx ctx'}` or\n  1398\t   `{:status :error :error e :log log :ctx ctx'}`. Either way `ctx'` has\n  1399\t   consumed the batch (`:t` + 1) and every attempt it allocated; only\n  1400\t   success changes the store, to the post-harvest store. A success also\n  1401\t   carries `:frontend-metadata` — the C1 side table finalized over the\n  1402\t   final tree (`final-call-site-metadata`), covering the tree that\n  1403\t   actually executes — when, and only when, the selected member itself\n  1404\t   claimed C1 coverage (its own verdict in `batch-call-site-claims`); a\n  1405\t   sibling's claim never manufactures a table for it, and an unclaimed\n  1406\t   batch carries no table at all, never an empty one. The admission\n  1407\t   this expansion produced the tree under rides beside it as\n  1408\t   `:call-site-origin` — the source origin of the admitted run member,\n  1409\t   the key the table is stored and resolved under beside the final\n  1410\t   root address. It is the table's admission key, not a blanket\n  1411\t   stamp: each row's origin is that occurrence's own (§2.1, §2.3) —\n  1412\t   a retained occurrence keeps its own incoming provenance (its\n  1413\t   source origin, or the generating expansion's, however deeply it\n  1414\t   was passed through), and generated syntax carries the\n  1415\t   `[:expansion record-address]` of the recorded expansion event\n  1416\t   whose output introduced it. A context\n  1417\t   store binding a\n  1418\t   reserved name, or holding an entry without the current AST contract,\n  1419\t   is refused (Rule R): it is a composition defect, so it throws rather\n  1420\t   than returning an error.\"\n  1421\t  [batch ctx]\n  1422\t  (check-store! (:store ctx))\n  1423\t  (let [ctx (with-default-guards ctx)\n  1424\t        source-batch (:t ctx)\n  1425\t        base {:ctx ctx, :source-batch source-batch, :events [], :produced []}\n  1426\t        finish (fn [st]\n  1427\t                 (let [ctx' (update (:ctx st) :t inc)]\n  1428\t                   (if-let [e (:error st)]\n  1429\t                     {:status :error, :error e, :log (log-packet st), :ctx ctx'}\n  1430\t                     {:status :ok, :tree (:tree st), :log (log-packet st),\n  1431\t                      :frontend-metadata (:frontend-metadata st),\n  1432\t                      :call-site-origin (:call-site-origin st),\n  1433\t                      :ctx (assoc ctx' :store (:next-store st))})))\n  1434\t        {:keys [admitted error]} (admit batch)]\n  1435\t    (if error\n  1436\t      (let [[st counter] (allocate-attempt base)]\n  1437\t        (finish (-> st\n  1438\t                    (record-event (event-row (attempt-id ctx counter) source-batch\n  1439\t                                             (source-origin ctx source-batch nil)\n  1440\t                                             nil nil nil nil nil error nil))\n  1441\t                    (fail error))))\n  1442\t      (let [{:keys [trees indexes index run-index definitions]} admitted\n  1443\t            store0 (or (:store ctx) {})\n  1444\t            store (harvest store0 #(nth indexes %) definitions)\n  1445\t            catalogue (into []\n  1446\t                            (comp (filter :declared?)\n  1447\t                                  (map (fn [{:keys [name tree path value]}]\n  1448\t                                         {:name name,\n  1449\t                                          :macro-tree (packet-of (nth indexes tree) value),\n  1450\t                                          :source [tree path]})))\n  1451\t                            definitions)\n  1452\t            ;; only the run tree is expanded, so only its declarations are\n  1453\t            ;; replaced; every catalogue entry still resolves by index\n  1454\t            [index standins]\n  1455\t            (reduce (fn [[index acc] [k {:keys [name source]}]]\n  1456\t                      (if (= run-index (first source))\n  1457\t                        (let [[index s] (intern-body index [standin-tag name k])]\n  1458\t                          [index (assoc acc (second source) s)])\n  1459\t                        [index acc]))\n  1460\t                    [index {}]\n  1461\t                    (map-indexed vector catalogue))\n  1462\t            [index root] (rebuild-paths index (first (nth trees run-index)) standins)\n  1463\t            st (assoc base :index index :store store)]\n  1464\t        (if-let [e (guard-batch-rows st)]\n  1465\t          (finish (fail st e))\n  1466\t          (let [[st root'] (expand-node st root\n  1467\t                                        {:path [], :rel [],\n  1468\t                                         :frame {:parent nil, :root root,\n  1469\t                                                 :tree-index run-index},\n  1470\t                                         :shadow #{}, :depth 0,\n  1471\t                                         ;; every syntax of the admitted\n  1472\t                                         ;; run tree starts as source\n  1473\t                                         ;; (§2.1); expansions override\n  1474\t                                         ;; below their outputs. The\n  1475\t                                         ;; function answers by absolute\n  1476\t                                         ;; occurrence path and ignores it\n  1477\t                                         ;; here: admitted syntax is all\n  1478\t                                         ;; source\n  1479\t                                         :origin-of\n  1480\t                                         (fn [_]\n  1481\t                                           (source-origin\n  1482\t                                             ctx source-batch run-index))})]\n  1483\t            (if (:error st)\n  1484\t              (finish st)\n  1485\t              (let [next-store (post-harvest store0 (:index st) root' catalogue)\n  1486\t                    [index root'] (retail (:index st) root')\n  1487\t                    [index root'] (lower-standins index root')\n  1488\t                    tree (packet-of index root')\n  1489\t                    ;; the ADMISSION origin of this expansion (§2.1):\n  1490\t                    ;; the admitted run member's source origin — the key\n  1491\t                    ;; the side table is stored and resolved under beside\n  1492\t                    ;; the final root address. It is NOT blindly stamped\n  1493\t                    ;; on every row: each row's own origin is the one the\n  1494\t                    ;; occurrence walk recorded (source for retained\n  1495\t                    ;; syntax, the generating event's `[:expansion …]`\n  1496\t                    ;; for generated syntax)\n  1497\t                    origin (source-origin ctx source-batch run-index)\n  1498\t                    ;; the selected member's own verdict decides its\n  1499\t                    ;; metadata; a sibling's claim never manufactures a\n  1500\t                    ;; table for a member that made none\n  1501\t                    claims (batch-call-site-claims batch)\n  1502\t                     metadata (when (and claims (nth claims run-index))\n  1503\t                                (final-call-site-metadata\n  1504\t                                  (packet->row-set tree)\n  1505\t                                  (:call-site-origins st) origin))]\n  1506\t                (if-let [e (valid-tree? tree)]\n  1507\t                  (throw (ex-info \"Expander produced a non-canonical tree\" e))\n  1508\t                  (finish (assoc st :tree tree :next-store next-store\n  1509\t                                 :frontend-metadata metadata\n  1510\t                                  :call-site-origin (when metadata origin))))))))))))\n  1511\t\n  1512\t\n  1513\t(defn expand\n  1514\t  \"`expand-batch` returning the tree packet, or throwing `ex-info` carrying\n  1515\t   the error data.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The twin-occurrence trace now separates the two histories: the retained branch delegates to the operand’s source origin, while the constructed branch gets the expansion origin despite sharing its address. I found the ruling in the main checkout; it’s absent from cc1. I’m checking whether other packet operations can lose that distinction and whether the metadata stays out of persisted values."}}
