",\"aggregated_output\":\"   721\\t\\n   722\\t\\n   723\\t(defn- standard-store\\n   724\\t  \\\"The expander store seeded with the standard forms, folded through the\\n   725\\t   same row-native batch contract as any input (yin.vm.macro.md §5.4).\\\"\\n   726\\t  []\\n   727\\t  (macro/seed-store (macro/make-ctx {:token :yin.repl/standard-forms\\n   728\\t                                     :source-medium :yin.repl/standard-forms})\\n   729\\t                    [macro/stdlib-forms]))\\n   730\\t\\n   731\\t\\n   732\\t(defn- make-expander\\n   733\\t  \\\"The expander consumer for one session: a fresh incarnation token, the\\n   734\\t   `program-in` identity as its source medium, the standard store, and the\\n   735\\t   `program-out` writer.  No log writer: `(compile ...)` renders events.\\\"\\n   736\\t  [program-identity program-out]\\n   737\\t  (macro/make-expander\\n   738\\t    (macro/make-ctx {:token (str (random-uuid))\\n   739\\t                     :source-medium program-identity\\n   740\\t                     :store (standard-store)})\\n   741\\t    program-out))\\n   742\\t\\n   743\\t\\n   744\\t(defn- make-session\\n   745\\t  \\\"Build the evaluator, its media, their attachments and observers, the\\n   746\\t   expander, and the loader the evaluator observer feeds the VM, together.\\n   747\\t   Reset and VM selection call this, so the whole composition is rebuilt as\\n   748\\t   one and each attachment capability is bound exactly once per medium\\n   749\\t   lifetime.\\n   750\\t\\n   751\\t   Both evaluators sit behind the same two stages (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1):\\n   752\\t   the expander observes `program-in` — `:program-stream`, watched by\\n   753\\t   `:observer` — and appends each expanded tree packet to `program-out` —\\n   754\\t   `:row-stream`, watched independently by the evaluator's `:row-observer`,\\n   755\\t   which loads each packet and runs it.  The code indexer's observer\\n   770\\t\\n   771\\t   A durable store's HEAD write travels with the store handle\\n   772\\t   (`:head-fn`, yin.repl.store): every session the store outlives\\n   773\\t   publishes through the same one.\\\"\\n   774\\t  [vm-type output-stream extra-primitives shell-token index-store source]\\n   775\\t  (let [linker (link/make source)\\n   776\\t        pair (:pair linker)\\n   777\\t        query-pair (query/make-pair query-pair-capacity)\\n   778\\t        vm (make-vm vm-type output-stream extra-primitives pair query-pair)\\n   779\\t        program-in (make-attachment ingress-capacity)\\n   780\\t        program-out (make-attachment ingress-capacity)]\\n   781\\t    {:vm vm\\n   782\\t     :load-program (get program-loaders vm-type)\\n   783\\t     :program-stream (:stream program-in)\\n   784\\t     :program-identity (:identity program-in)\\n   785\\t     :observer (:observer program-in)\\n   786\\t     :expander (make-expander (:identity program-in) (:stream program-out))\\n   787\\t     :row-stream (:stream program-out)\\n   788\\t     :row-observer (:observer program-out)\\n   789\\t     :indexer (index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))\\n   790\\t                                   :session-token shell-token\\n   548\\t            by their origin+root pair (design §2.1, K = [origin root\\n   549\\t            path])\\\"\\n   550\\t    (let [store (macro/seed-store\\n   551\\t                  (macro/make-ctx {:token :callsite-test/standard-forms\\n   552\\t                                   :source-medium :callsite-test/standard-forms})\\n   553\\t                  [macro/stdlib-forms])\\n   554\\t          ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \\\"callsite-test\\\"\\n   555\\t                               :source-medium :program-in\\n   556\\t                               :store store})\\n   557\\t          ast (yang/compile-program '[(defn f [x] (+ x 1)) (f 2)])\\n   558\\t          first-origin [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]\\n   559\\t          consumer (macro/make-expander ctx nil)\\n   560\\t          consumer (macro/load consumer (encoder/program-batch ast))\\n   561\\t          first-tree (:out-staged consumer)\\n   562\\t          second-origin [:source :program-in (:t (:ctx consumer)) 0]\\n   563\\t          consumer (macro/load consumer (encoder/program-batch ast))\\n   564\\t          second-tree (:out-staged consumer)]\\n   565\\t      ;; the load that exposes the defect: identical programs, so the\\n   566\\t      ;; final trees are content-identical — same root\\n   567\\t      (is (= (first first-tree) (first second-tree))\\n   568\\t          \\\"two admissions produced the same root address\\\")\\n   569\\t      (is (not= first-origin second-origin)\\n   570\\t          \\\"the two admissions are different occurrence origins\\\")\\n   571\\t      (testing \\\"each occurrence's table resolves under its own origin\\\"\\n   572\\t        (doseq [[label tree admission]\\n   573\\t                [[\\\"first\\\" first-tree first-origin]\\n   574\\t                 [\\\"second\\\" second-tree second-origin]]]\\n   575\\t          (let [rows (macro/call-site-table consumer tree admission)]\\n   576\\t            (is (seq rows) (str label \\\" load's table resolves\\\"))\\n   577\\t            (is (= (occurrence-pairs (macro/packet->row-set tree))\\n   578\\t                   (marked-pairs rows)))\\n   579\\t            (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\\n   580\\t                         (macro/packet->row-set tree) rows admission\\n1680:        tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\\n1703:        tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\\n1715:      tail? (assoc :tail? true))\\n1723:      tail? (assoc :tail? true))\\n1751:         tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))\\n1769:       tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\\n1794:     tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\\n1830:        tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\\n1853:           tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))))\\n1931:                                                tail? (assoc :tail? true))}\\n1933:                      tail? (assoc :tail? true))))]\\n1952:     :tail? true}))\\n2431:                         tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\\n2444:                         tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\\n2456:                       tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n26:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"NOT ENDORSED\\n\\nAssessed `d91489f7` against U1–U3 as requested. U2 resolves the prior admission-default objection; U1’s implementation premise remains false.\\n\\n- **U1 / P1-a — not satisfied.** `expand-call` builds an input **address set**, then assigns incoming provenance to any output whose address belongs to that set ([macro.cljc:1087](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1087), [macro.cljc:1140](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1140)). This still classifies provenance by content equality. Consider a macro returning an `if` containing both an admitted `(f 1)` operand and a freshly constructed identical `(f 1)`. Both receive the source origin; the constructed application should name the expansion event. Their different final paths distinguish positions, but do not correctly identify their different histories.\\n\\n  Recording that result by path does not repair the classification ([macro.cljc:1200](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1200)). Expansion records retain attempt, parent, input root, call path, macro root and output root, but no per-output-occurrence retention/generation correspondence ([macro.cljc:1005](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1005)). U1 requires history-derived origins; it does not authorize this address-membership inference.\\n\\n- **U2 / P1-b — satisfied for C1 publication.** Explicit admission tokens take precedence, scoped calls allocate distinct ordinals, and undeclared identical publication uses the deterministic default ([publish.cljc:277](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:277)). Under U2, that default is correct. The previous keyword-namespace/type collision is fixed by `pr-str` ([publish.cljc:136](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:136)). Origins are persisted and retrieved from the record ([publish.cljc:327](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:327), [publish.cljc:450](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:450)). Distinct events are representable, with scope uniqueness and replay identity owned by the composition.\\n\\n- **Site-table identity — structurally sound, insufficient to establish provenance.** Tables are partitioned by admission origin and final root; rows additionally carry occurrence paths ([macro.cljc:1491](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1491)). This preserves correctly supplied distinctions. It cannot recover the generating origin incorrectly replaced with a source origin above.\\n\\n- **Multi-claim validator / P2 — closed.** Every validator mode now rejects multiple origins claiming one `[root path]` within a single coverage table, reporting both claims ([clojure.cljc:199](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:199)). This checks consistency, not historical truth.\\n\\n- **Additional U1/U3 gap — record retention is not guaranteed.** `macro/load` retains the returned expansion log only when a log writer exists ([macro.cljc:1522](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1522)); the production REPL explicitly constructs its expander without one ([repl.cljc:732](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:732)). Consequently, retained site rows can name expansion-record addresses whose records this path does not retain. The ruling’s premise of queryable retained history does not itself supply that retention.\\n\\nNo files modified; no tests run.\"}}\n(defn- slot-of\n  [tree n]\n  (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/slot tree))\n        kinds (into {} (slot-kinds (row-tag row)))\n        index (packet-index tree)]\n    (when-not (and (integer? n) (contains? kinds n))\n      (throw-prelude \"yin/slot position names no grammar slot\"\n                     {:op 'yin/slot, :position n}))\n    (case (get kinds n)\n      :node (packet-of index (nth row n))\n      :nodes (mapv #(packet-of index %) (nth row n))\n      (nth row n))))\n\n\n(defn prelude\n  \"The closed body environment (§5.3): the pure standard primitives (no\n   `require`, no stream or FFI constructor) and the row-native constructors,\n   each consuming and returning self-contained tree packets. `gensym` is the\n   invocation-local `yin/gensym-sym`.\"\n  [gensym]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
