{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"NOT ENDORSED\n\nThe original P1-a counterexample is repaired, but round 5 introduces two concrete regressions and leaves the retained-history gap open. Static review of `847aa885`; no files changed or tests run.\n\n1. **Address-membership inference: removed.** `expand-call` now obtains origins from occurrence paths and the recorded correspondence. Remaining address comparisons handle content interning/deduplication, not origin classification. See [macro.cljc:1206](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1206), [macro.cljc:1258](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1258), and [macro.cljc:1313](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1313).\n\n2. **Construction history: correct for the counterexample.** For `if true x (fresh-f-1)`, coordinate `3` delegates to `x`’s incoming source origin; coordinate `4` delegates to the newly constructed application’s pending expansion origin. Equal content addresses do not merge these coordinate-specific functions. The resulting correspondence is `{[3] [:retained source], [4] :constructed}`; field 12 retains it, and the walk resolves `:constructed` to that record’s address. See [macro.cljc:627](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:627), [macro.cljc:654](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:654), [macro.cljc:1157](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1157), and [macro.cljc:1083](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1083).\n\n3. **Metadata isolation: incomplete; concrete regression.** Ordinary constructor composition excludes packet metadata from row bodies, and successful final packets/store entries are rebuilt without that wrapper metadata ([macro.cljc:1485](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1485), [macro.cljc:1022](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1022)). However, `(defmacro capture [x] (yin/literal x))` now passes an annotated packet into a literal’s content body ([macro.cljc:667](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:667)). **Jing hashes collection metadata** and encounters the origin function, which its encoder rejects ([cbor.cljc:834](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:834), [cbor.cljc:904](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:904)). Thus metadata reaches content encoding and breaks previously plain packet-as-data usage; it does not silently persist into a successful final tree.\n\n4. **Tests: pin the original bug, not the full U1 contract.** The test establishes equal addresses, two paths, distinct source/expansion origins, and the exact recorded correspondence ([clojure_callsite_test.cljc:496](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:496), [clojure_callsite_test.cljc:513](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:513), [clojure_callsite_test.cljc:522](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:522)). The final-table assertions collect an **origin set**, however: swapping the two branches’ origins would still pass. Assert each final branch’s specific origin and generating record. The regressions above/below are also uncovered.\n\n5. **Nested/final paths: core logic sound, slot extraction regressed.** Absolute-prefix composition preserves the operand’s own origin through nested pass-through. Tail marking and stand-in lowering preserve application coordinates, so final-path lookup remains appropriate ([macro.cljc:1210](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1210), [macro.cljc:942](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:942), [macro.cljc:1387](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1387)). But `slot-of :nodes` changed from a vector to lazy `map-indexed` ([macro.cljc:725](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:725)). Consequently, `(get (yin/slot x 3) 0)` now returns nil rather than the first operand packet; `get` is the exposed host primitive ([vm.cljc:402](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:402)). Preserve the vector result.\n\n**Residual gaps:** U1/U3 history recovery remains incomplete in the production REPL: `load` retains expansion records only with a log writer, while the REPL supplies none ([macro.cljc:1646](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1646), [repl.cljc:732](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:732)). Also update the documented eleven-field event schema for the new correspondence field ([yin.vm.macro.md:675](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:675)). U2 is unaffected by this diff."}}
